# Provider Layer Rules

## Contract First

- **Do not** call a third-party SDK or API directly from modules. All external calls go through `app/providers/<payment|otp|meeting>/`.
- Each provider folder has a **base** module defining an abstract class (ABC) with a fixed set of methods and return types (e.g. dataclasses or Pydantic models). The rest of the app depends only on this contract.

## Adding a New Provider

1. Implement the **same** methods and return types as in `base.py` (same names, same semantics).
2. Add a new file, e.g. `app/providers/payment/stripe.py`, and implement the ABC.
3. In `factory.py`, add a branch for the new name (e.g. from `PAYMENT_PROVIDER=stripe`) and return the new class. No changes in modules that use the provider.

## Implementation Details

- Use `app.config.settings` for keys/URLs; never hardcode secrets.
- Normalize errors into `app.core.exceptions.ProviderError` (or the same pattern) so callers see a consistent API.
- Keep provider-specific types (e.g. Razorpay order payload) inside the provider module; the public contract uses our own dataclasses/schemas (e.g. `PaymentOrder`, `MeetingDetails`).

## Existing Providers

- **payment**: `create_order`, `verify_payment`, `initiate_refund` → `PaymentOrder`, `PaymentVerification`, `RefundResult`
- **otp**: `send_otp(phone, otp)` → bool
- **meeting**: `create_meeting`, `get_join_url`, `cancel_meeting` → `MeetingDetails` / str / bool
